---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Car problems by model year, from NHTSA complaints and recalls
---
{%- set top = nhtsa.modelYears | sort(true, false, "s.total") -%}
<section class="hero">
<h1>Car problems by make, model and year, counted from NHTSA data</h1>
<p class="lede">How many owner complaints and safety recalls the U.S. National Highway Traffic Safety Administration (NHTSA) lists for each model year, which parts owners complain about most, and every recall campaign number. No opinions, no star ratings: just NHTSA's public records, counted, with the source link and date on every page.</p>
</section>
<div id="search" class="search"></div>
<noscript><p><a href="/makes/">Browse all makes</a></p></noscript>

<h2>Most-complained-about model years on this site</h2>
<div class="tablewrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Model year</th><th class="num">Complaints</th><th class="num">Recalls</th><th>Most-named component</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for y in top | batch(12) | first %}<tr><td><a href="{{ y.url }}">{{ y.name }}</a></td><td class="num">{{ y.s.total | n }}</td><td class="num">{{ y.s.recalls.length }}</td><td>{{ y.s.named[0].label }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>
<p class="muted">Raw counts from NHTSA, checked {{ nhtsa.checked | prettyDate }}. Popular cars collect more complaints simply because more were sold. This list is not a reliability or safety ranking. Compare years within one model first.</p>

{% if nhtsa.topics.length %}
<h2>One component across model years</h2>
<p class="muted">These pages follow a single NHTSA component group for one model. Owner complaints and recall campaigns are counted separately. A complaint count is not the number of vehicles in a recall.</p>
<ul class="cards">
{% for t in nhtsa.topics %}<li><a href="{{ t.url }}"><strong>{{ t.name }} {{ t.labelLower }}</strong><span>{{ t.complaintNaming | n }} complaints name this group · {{ t.recalls.length }} matching recall campaigns · checked {{ t.checked | prettyDate }}</span></a></li>{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% endif %}

<h2>Models</h2>
<div class="brands">
{% for mk in nhtsa.makes %}<div class="brand-card"><h3><a href="{{ mk.url }}">{{ mk.make }}</a></h3>
<p class="models-line">{% for m in mk.models %}<a href="{{ m.url }}">{{ m.model }}</a> <span class="muted">(most complaints: {{ m.rankable[0].year }})</span>{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p></div>
{% endfor %}
</div>

<section class="how">
<h2>What the numbers are</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Complaints</strong> are reports owners file with NHTSA about a safety problem. NHTSA publishes them; it does not verify each one.</li>
<li><strong>Recalls</strong> are campaigns where an automaker or NHTSA has found a safety defect; the fix is normally free at a dealer. Look up your own car by VIN at <a href="https://www.nhtsa.gov/recalls" rel="nofollow noopener">nhtsa.gov/recalls</a>.</li>
<li>All counts come from NHTSA's free public APIs and are recounted when the data is refreshed. <a href="/about/">Full method</a>.</li>
</ul>
</section>
